# Witnessed acts (K1, DESIGN.md §10.1). Riverhold's knowledge model is "witnessed": only
# those who learn of an act firsthand change their minds. That's the witnesses, the parties
# the act names, and the factions of the characters among them, but never through the actor.

load content/sample

# The player picks Hale's pocket, seen only by Merchant Ava. Hale didn't notice, so neither
# he nor the Watch knows: the alignment moves, the standings don't.
act player steal --target captain_hale --seen-by merchant_ava --explain
assert show character player == player — The Player — law -5.00, good -3.00 — True Neutral
assert standing player == no standing with anyone yet

# Caught in the act: Hale sees it, and the Watch learns through him. −10.00 with the Watch
# spills +1.80 to the Guild (−0.18 at −80) and −1.00 to the Temple (0.10 at +60).
act player steal --target captain_hale --seen-by captain_hale --explain
assert standing player captain_hale == -20.00
assert standing player city_watch == -10.00
assert standing player lantern_guild == 1.80
assert standing player temple == -1.00

# A donation reaches the Temple, which it names, even unseen: +10.00, spilling +1.00 to the
# Watch and −2.40 to the Ashen Circle (−0.24 at −90).
act player donate_to_temple --unseen --explain
assert standing player temple == 9.00
assert standing player city_watch == -9.00
assert standing player ashen_circle == -2.40
